# Make a Release (fork panel)

When the user says **make a release** (or equivalent), create a GitHub Release for this fork so production can upgrade via tarball — not `pterodactyl/panel`.

## Context

- Fork: `https://github.com/jackh54/panel`
- Upstream: `https://github.com/pterodactyl/panel`
- Release workflow: `.github/workflows/release.yaml` (runs on `v*` tags, builds assets, uploads `panel.tar.gz`)
- Do **not** use official: `https://github.com/pterodactyl/panel/releases/latest/download/panel.tar.gz`

## Steps

1. Confirm working tree is clean enough to tag (warn if dirty; do not commit unless asked).
2. Choose next tag: `vX.Y.Z` or fork-style `vX.Y.Z-jack.N`. Prefer bumping from latest existing `v*` tag on `origin`.
3. Ensure branch is pushed to `origin`, then create and push the tag:
   ```bash
   git tag <tag>
   git push origin <tag>
   ```
4. Wait for the **Release** GitHub Action to finish and confirm `panel.tar.gz` is on the release.
5. Give the user copy-paste **update commands** (one block each), adapted from https://pterodactyl.io/panel/1.0/updating.html, using this fork’s URL.

## Update commands to give the user

Replace `<tag>` with the tag just published (or use `latest` once the release is published).

```bash
cd /var/www/pterodactyl
```

```bash
php artisan down
```

```bash
curl -L https://github.com/jackh54/panel/releases/latest/download/panel.tar.gz | tar -xzv
```

(Or pin: `https://github.com/jackh54/panel/releases/download/<tag>/panel.tar.gz`)

```bash
chmod -R 755 storage/* bootstrap/cache
```

```bash
composer install --no-dev --optimize-autoloader
```

```bash
php artisan view:clear
```

```bash
php artisan config:clear
```

```bash
php artisan migrate --seed --force
```

```bash
# NGINX/Apache (not CentOS):
chown -R www-data:www-data /var/www/pterodactyl/*
# CentOS NGINX: chown -R nginx:nginx /var/www/pterodactyl/*
# CentOS Apache: chown -R apache:apache /var/www/pterodactyl/*
```

```bash
php artisan queue:restart
```

```bash
php artisan up
```

Remind them to upgrade Wings if the Panel/Wings version matrix requires it.

## Do not

- Point upgrade curl at `pterodactyl/panel`
- Force-push tags or skip hooks unless explicitly asked
- Commit/push unrelated changes as part of release unless asked
